# rsync_backup_scripts
#
# This file replaced a 429-line Visual Studio template that inverted BOTH
# halves of this repo's commit policy:
#
#   * `Backup*/` matched `backups/` on any case-insensitive filesystem
#     (macOS APFS, git core.ignorecase=true), so the generated runners -- which
#     MUST be committed -- were invisible to `git add` on the MacBook while
#     being perfectly visible on the case-sensitive Ubuntu box. The same repo
#     tracked a different set of files on the two machines.
#   * `config/` was NOT ignored, so paths, usernames, hostnames and Tailscale
#     IPs would have been committed.
#
# Do not paste a language/IDE template back in here without re-checking:
#     git check-ignore -v backups/<name>.sh config/<name>/source.txt

# Machine-specific configuration. Never commit: paths, usernames, hosts, IPs.
config/*
backups/*

# Per-run logs and run state. Never commit.
/logs/

# Remote-server definitions: hosts and paths. Machine-specific, never commit.
/remotes/

# backups/ is ignored too. The generated runners contain nothing
# machine-specific -- a backup name plus a call into lib/common.sh -- but they
# are useless without their config/<name>/, which is ignored, so a committed
# runner on another machine only fails with "no configuration, run setup.sh".
# setup.sh regenerates them per machine, so there is nothing to preserve.

.DS_Store
._*
*~
*.swp

CLAUDE.md

# GUI build artifacts (anchored on purpose -- see the template warning above).
/gui/build/
/gui/dist/
/gui/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc